1031
01:21:59,683 --> 01:22:01,708
Oh, no, no. That's not what happened.

1032
01:22:02,085 --> 01:22:04,815
What happened was there was this party at my parents'.

1033
01:22:04,988 --> 01:22:07,422
- I drove your mother home... - I don't want to hear this!

1034
01:22:07,491 --> 01:22:09,755
- We went upstairs to see your portrait... - No! I don't!

1035
01:22:09,826 --> 01:22:11,987
- She started taking her clothes off, - This is my mother, Benjamin!

1036
01:22:12,095 --> 01:22:15,496
And suddenly, there she was without any clothes on... I mean, really naked.

1037
01:22:15,599 --> 01:22:17,931
Oh, shut... aah!

1038
01:22:31,615 --> 01:22:33,879
- Oh, hello, Mr. Mccleery. - Who screamed?

1039
01:22:33,950 --> 01:22:35,417
It's all right, Mr. Mccleery.

1040
01:22:35,519 --> 01:22:38,044
Screaming is not all right, not in my house, It isn't.

1041
01:22:38,221 --> 01:22:40,621
It was just a visitor, but it's all right now.

1042
01:22:42,726 --> 01:22:44,091
What did you do to her?

1043
01:22:44,327 --> 01:22:47,421
Look, she's all right. She's upset, and she screamed, but it's ok now.

1044
01:22:47,531 --> 01:22:49,021
- Shall I get the cops? - What?

1045
01:22:49,132 --> 01:22:50,861
- I' II get the cops. - Hey, wait a minute.

1046
01:22:51,268 --> 01:22:52,496
Now, damn it, look.

1047
01:22:53,370 --> 01:22:55,031
Here she is, having some water.

1048
01:22:56,440 --> 01:22:58,431
There's no need for the cops or anything.

1049
01:22:58,642 --> 01:23:01,440
All right, boys, you can all go back to your rooms now.

1050
01:23:01,945 --> 01:23:03,173
Go ahead.

1051
01:23:03,747 --> 01:23:05,840
We won't have any more of this agitation.

1052
01:23:07,751 --> 01:23:09,685
- Will we, Braddock? - No, sir.

1053
01:23:12,889 --> 01:23:14,447
I want you out of here.

1054
01:23:15,158 --> 01:23:17,251
- What do you mean? - You heard me out of here.

1055
01:23:17,360 --> 01:23:19,590
- What for? - Because I don't like you.

1056
01:23:52,596 --> 01:23:54,257
I'm sorry I screamed.

1057
01:23:58,702 --> 01:24:01,000
Benjamin, when you came up here,

1058
01:24:01,104 --> 01:24:03,231
what did you think was going to happen between us?

1059
01:24:05,208 --> 01:24:07,676
Elaine, right now I don't feel like talking much.

1060
01:24:07,744 --> 01:24:10,872
I'm sorry about everything, but I think I' II just do this now.

1061
01:24:22,759 --> 01:24:24,886
Can I just sit here while you're packing?

1062
01:24:40,377 --> 01:24:42,004
What are you going to do now?

1063
01:24:43,246 --> 01:24:44,736
I don't know.

1064
01:24:45,448 --> 01:24:47,780
- Are you going home? - No.

1065
01:24:47,984 --> 01:24:49,815
Well, where are you going?

1066
01:24:53,790 --> 01:24:55,951
Elaine, you're going to have to stop asking me that.

1067
01:25:09,172 --> 01:25:11,003
I don't want you to leave tomorrow.

1068
01:25:14,110 --> 01:25:15,668
I don't understand.

1069
01:25:16,079 --> 01:25:17,740
I don't want you to go anywhere...

1070
01:25:20,984 --> 01:25:22,747
Until you have a definite plan.

1071
01:25:23,520 --> 01:25:25,215
Good-bye.

1072
01:26:00,957 --> 01:26:02,549
What's happening?

1073
01:26:02,759 --> 01:26:04,454
- Benjamin? - What?

1074
01:26:10,433 --> 01:26:11,923
Will you kiss me?

1075
01:26:39,663 --> 01:26:41,255
Will you marry me?

1076
01:26:44,768 --> 01:26:47,259
- You won't? - I don't know.

1077
01:26:50,273 --> 01:26:51,934
But you might?

1078
01:26:53,076 --> 01:26:54,600
I might.

1079
01:26:54,911 --> 01:26:56,469
Is that so?

1080
01:26:57,080 --> 01:26:59,514
- You might marry me? - Yes.

1081
01:27:00,684 --> 01:27:02,174
When?

1082
01:27:03,319 --> 01:27:04,946
I don't know.

1083
01:27:05,221 --> 01:27:07,621
How about tomorrow? I don't mean to be pushy.

1084
01:27:07,724 --> 01:27:09,453
I don't know.

1085
01:27:10,527 --> 01:27:12,586
I don't know what's happening.

1086
01:27:14,597 --> 01:27:16,292
You mean you're confused?

1087
01:27:19,002 --> 01:27:20,663
Look, don't be confused.

1088
01:27:21,504 --> 01:27:23,028
We're getting married.

1089
01:27:24,808 --> 01:27:26,332
I don't see how we can.

1090
01:27:29,913 --> 01:27:31,505
We just can.

1091
01:27:39,022 --> 01:27:40,512
I have to go now.

1092
01:27:41,925 --> 01:27:43,256
Hey, Elaine?

1093
01:27:44,961 --> 01:27:46,656
Are you serious about this?

1094
01:27:48,031 --> 01:27:49,430
I'll think about it.

1095
01:27:49,866 --> 01:27:51,925
- You really will? - Yes.

1096
01:28:05,081 --> 01:28:06,571
Good god.

1097
01:28:08,551 --> 01:28:10,746
We can go get our blood tests tomorrow.

1098
01:28:10,787 --> 01:28:12,311
- Tomorrow? - Or this afternoon.

1099
01:28:12,355 --> 01:28:13,549
It's a good day for it.

1100
01:28:13,590 --> 01:28:16,059
Benjamin, I haven't even said I' II marry you yet.

1101
01:28:16,059 --> 01:28:17,458
We'll need our birth certificates.

1102
01:28:17,560 --> 01:28:20,358
I happen to have mine with me. Where's yours?

1103
01:28:20,764 --> 01:28:23,028
- I just don't think it would work. - Why wouldn't it?

1104
01:28:35,078 --> 01:28:38,013
- Why wouldn't it? - I just don't think it would.

1105
01:28:39,482 --> 01:28:42,645
Tomorrow, then. Can we get our blood tests tomorrow morning?

1106
01:28:43,720 --> 01:28:46,883
Why don't you just drag me off if you want to marry me so much?

1107
01:28:46,990 --> 01:28:48,890
Why don't I just drag you off?

1108
01:28:48,992 --> 01:28:52,155
All right. I will, right after we get the blood tests.

1109
01:28:52,529 --> 01:28:54,394
I have to see Carl first.

1110
01:28:54,497 --> 01:28:56,226
Carl who?

1111
01:28:59,402 --> 01:29:01,199
Carl who?

1112
01:29:01,604 --> 01:29:04,767
Carl smith. He's a medical student. We've known him for years.

1113
01:29:04,908 --> 01:29:06,933
- Who, that guy at the zoo? - Yes.

1114
01:29:07,010 --> 01:29:10,002
- Why do you have to see him? - Well, I said I might marry him.

1115
01:29:11,948 --> 01:29:13,472
You what?!

1116
01:29:13,817 --> 01:29:15,478
How did he do it?

1117
01:29:15,618 --> 01:29:17,210
Did he get down on his knees?

1118
01:29:17,320 --> 01:29:19,220
He didn't get down on his knees, I hope.

1119
01:29:19,255 --> 01:29:20,813
No, Benjamin.

1120
01:29:20,924 --> 01:29:23,017
What did he say? I'm curious.

1121
01:29:23,126 --> 01:29:24,525
Shh.

1122
01:29:24,627 --> 01:29:27,926
He said he thought we'd make a pretty good team.

1123
01:29:28,131 --> 01:29:31,225
- Oh, no. He said that? - Shh!

1124
01:29:31,334 --> 01:29:32,892
Where did he do it?

1125
01:29:34,571 --> 01:29:36,766
I'd like to know where it happened.

1126
01:29:39,642 --> 01:29:41,667
It wasn't in his car, was it?

1127
01:29:55,058 --> 01:29:56,457
Good night.

1128
01:29:56,593 --> 01:29:58,959
Are we getting married tomorrow?

1129
01:29:59,596 --> 01:30:00,961
No.

1130
01:30:02,065 --> 01:30:03,623
The day after tomorrow?

1131
01:30:05,401 --> 01:30:08,734
I don't know. Maybe we are, and maybe we're not.

1132
01:30:59,222 --> 01:31:02,555
Do you want to, uh... do you want to try and tell me why you did it?

1133
01:31:04,427 --> 01:31:05,826
Mr. Robinson.

1134
01:31:06,029 --> 01:31:07,860
Do you have a special grudge against me?

1135
01:31:07,964 --> 01:31:10,262
Do you feel a particularly strong resentment?

1136
01:31:10,333 --> 01:31:11,425
No.

1137
01:31:11,534 --> 01:31:13,661
Is there something I' ve said that's caused this contempt,

1138
01:31:13,736 --> 01:31:16,500
or is it just things I stand for that you despise?

1139
01:31:16,639 --> 01:31:18,266
It was nothing to do with you, sir.

1140
01:31:18,374 --> 01:31:21,366
Well, Ben, it was quite a bit to do with me.

1141
01:31:21,444 --> 01:31:22,934
Now, look, please...

1142
01:31:23,046 --> 01:31:24,741
Ben, I think we're 2 civilized human beings.

1143
01:31:24,847 --> 01:31:26,678
Do you think it's necessary to threaten each other?

1144
01:31:26,749 --> 01:31:28,239
I'm not threatening you.

1145
01:31:28,351 --> 01:31:31,047
Do you want to unclench your fist, please? Thank you.

1146
01:31:31,254 --> 01:31:33,779
I can see in the dark, you know. I've been here quite a while.

1147
01:31:34,090 --> 01:31:37,651
I'm trying to tell you I have no personal feelings about you, Mr. Robinson.

1148
01:31:37,760 --> 01:31:39,694
I'm trying to tell you I do not resent you.

1149
01:31:39,762 --> 01:31:42,287
You don't respect me terribly much, either.

1150
01:31:43,199 --> 01:31:44,757
- No, sir. - What?

1151
01:31:44,968 --> 01:31:47,562
- No, sir. - Don't shout at me, Ben.

1152
01:31:47,670 --> 01:31:50,332
I may not be as young as you, but I still have pretty good hearing.

1153
01:31:50,373 --> 01:31:53,706
- Mr. Robinson... - Have the decency to wait until I finish.

1154
01:31:54,978 --> 01:31:57,538
I do think you should know the consequences of what you've done.

1155
01:31:57,680 --> 01:32:01,081
I do think you should know that my wife and I are getting a divorce soon.

1156
01:32:01,484 --> 01:32:02,951
But why?

1157
01:32:02,986 --> 01:32:04,419
Why?!

1158
01:32:04,520 --> 01:32:06,044
Listen to me.

1159
01:32:06,823 --> 01:32:09,849
What happened between Mrs. Robinson and me was nothing.

1160
01:32:10,026 --> 01:32:11,618
It didn't mean anything.

1161
01:32:11,728 --> 01:32:15,220
We might just as well have been shaking hands.

1162
01:32:15,398 --> 01:32:16,956
Shaking hands.

1163
01:32:17,100 --> 01:32:19,364
That's not saying much for my wife, is it?

1164
01:32:19,402 --> 01:32:21,632
- You miss the point. - I guess I do.

1165
01:32:21,704 --> 01:32:24,537
The point is, I don't love your wife. Ilove your daughter, sir.

1166
01:32:25,541 --> 01:32:27,509
All right. Now listen to this.

1167
01:32:27,710 --> 01:32:30,611
I don't know whether I can prosecute, but I think I can.

1168
01:32:30,747 --> 01:32:34,513
I think I can get you behind bars if you ever look at my daughter again.

1169
01:32:34,951 --> 01:32:37,920
I've seen Elaine, and I' ve made damn sure you can't get to her.

1170
01:32:38,021 --> 01:32:39,488
Stay away from me, Ben!

1171
01:32:40,723 --> 01:32:42,486
I don't want to mince words with you.

1172
01:32:42,558 --> 01:32:46,824
As far as Elaine is concerned, you're to get her out of your filthy mind right now.

1173
01:32:46,929 --> 01:32:49,363
Is that perfectly clear to you?

1174
01:32:49,532 --> 01:32:53,935
And that's all, Ben. You'll pardon me if I don't shake hands with you.

1175
01:32:55,938 --> 01:32:57,963
I think you are filth.

1176
01:32:58,174 --> 01:33:00,472
I think you are scum!

1177
01:33:02,145 --> 01:33:03,840
You are a degenerate!

1178
01:33:09,852 --> 01:33:11,114
Hi.

1179
01:33:13,456 --> 01:33:16,448
Mr. Mccleery, do you have some change? I need to use the phone.

1180
01:33:16,759 --> 01:33:18,659
I want you out of here.

1181
01:33:18,861 --> 01:33:22,262
Look, I' II give you $10 for a dime. I'll give you 20.

1182
01:33:23,066 --> 01:33:25,398
For god's sake, will you let me use that phone?

1183
01:33:26,269 --> 01:33:28,499
I'm going to call the police... now.

1184
01:33:28,571 --> 01:33:30,562
Could I make one phone call first?

1185
01:33:30,773 --> 01:33:32,400
Get out of here!

1186
01:33:43,419 --> 01:33:45,819
Elaine Robinson has left school

1187
01:33:46,422 --> 01:33:49,255
Her roommate's coming down with a note for you.

1188
01:33:52,795 --> 01:33:54,990
Dear Benjamin, please forgive me,

1189
01:33:55,331 --> 01:33:58,391
because I know what I' m doing is the best thing for you.

1190
01:33:58,701 --> 01:34:01,261
My father is so upset. You've got to understand.

1191
01:34:01,637 --> 01:34:03,502
Ilove you, but it would never work out.

1192
01:35:27,990 --> 01:35:29,480
Elaine?

1193
01:35:31,627 --> 01:35:33,219
Hello, Benjamin.

1194
01:35:37,600 --> 01:35:38,828
Where is she?

1195
01:35:39,001 --> 01:35:41,196
- Hello. Get me the police, please. - Where's Elaine?

1196
01:35:41,304 --> 01:35:42,828
I'll be with you in a moment, Benjamin.

1197
01:35:42,939 --> 01:35:46,431
Do you have a patrol car in the vicinity of 1200 glenview road?

1198
01:35:47,310 --> 01:35:48,834
Good. We have a burglar here.

1199
01:35:49,512 --> 01:35:51,742
Just a second. I' II ask him. Are you armed?

1200
01:35:53,716 --> 01:35:55,377
No, I don't believe he is.

1201
01:35:55,518 --> 01:35:56,746
Thank you.

1202
01:35:57,153 --> 01:35:58,677
What have you done to her?

1203
01:35:58,821 --> 01:36:01,619
I think we have everything quite under control now, Benjamin.

1204
01:36:01,657 --> 01:36:03,386
Would you like a quick drink before you go?

1205
01:36:03,459 --> 01:36:06,189
You can't stop me from seeing her. I'll find her.

1206
01:36:06,629 --> 01:36:09,393
Sorry we won't be able to invite you to the wedding Benjamin,

1207
01:36:09,432 --> 01:36:11,366
but the arrangements have been so rushed.

1208
01:36:12,568 --> 01:36:14,559
What the hell have you...

1209
01:36:19,542 --> 01:36:22,943
I don't think you'll have time for that drink after all.

1210
01:36:23,980 --> 01:36:26,744
- I' II find her. - I don't think so.

1211
01:37:30,946 --> 01:37:32,538
Say, fellas.

1212
01:37:33,616 --> 01:37:36,244
Do any of you fellas know where carl smith is?

1213
01:37:36,452 --> 01:37:38,943
He took off in the middle of the night to get married.

1214
01:37:39,121 --> 01:37:41,282
Probably one step ahead of the shotgun.

1215
01:37:42,224 --> 01:37:44,249
Would you happen to know where he's getting married?

1216
01:37:44,360 --> 01:37:45,952
I'm supposed to be there.

1217
01:37:46,062 --> 01:37:47,552
Why don't you ask Carter?

1218
01:37:48,331 --> 01:37:50,265
Would you happen to know where I might find him?

1219
01:37:50,366 --> 01:37:51,993
Hey, Carter!

1220
01:37:52,968 --> 01:37:55,061
Where's the make-out king getting married?

1221
01:37:55,171 --> 01:37:57,196
Santa barbara!

1222
01:37:57,340 --> 01:37:58,739
You don't happen to know exactly...

1223
01:37:58,841 --> 01:38:01,105
where the old make-out king is getting married, do you?

1224
01:38:01,243 --> 01:38:02,767
I'm supposed to be there.

1225
01:38:02,878 --> 01:38:04,937
Where in santa barbara?

1226
01:38:05,748 --> 01:38:10,208
I don't know. Maybe his old man's house, or in the maternity ward.

1227
01:38:11,387 --> 01:38:13,514
- Hey, you going to the wedding? - Yeah.

1228
01:38:13,589 --> 01:38:15,955
Hey, tell him to save a piece for me.

1229
01:38:17,460 --> 01:38:19,052
Of the wedding cake!

1230
01:39:05,007 --> 01:39:07,601
- Can I use your phone? - Yeah.

1231
01:39:34,870 --> 01:39:36,394
Hello, who is this?

1232
01:39:36,472 --> 01:39:38,201
This is Dr. Smith's answering service.

1233
01:39:38,274 --> 01:39:39,639
Is the doctor anywhere?

1234
01:39:39,742 --> 01:39:42,233
I'm afraid the doctor can't be reached right now. If you'd like to leave...

1235
01:39:42,344 --> 01:39:43,902
I have to know where he is.

1236
01:39:44,046 --> 01:39:47,709
Well, the doctor is at his son's wedding, but I' m sure it's over by now.

1237
01:39:47,950 --> 01:39:49,315
He should be checking in at any moment.

1238
01:39:49,452 --> 01:39:51,784
Listen to me. I'm Dr. Smith's brother,

1239
01:39:52,054 --> 01:39:54,955
reverend smith, and I' m supposed to perform the ceremony.

1240
01:39:55,057 --> 01:39:58,151
I just got in from Portland, and I' ve forgotten what church, you see?

1241
01:39:58,294 --> 01:40:03,596
Well, I' m not sure, but you might try the first presbyterian. That's on allan street.

1242
01:40:03,666 --> 01:40:05,395
Thank you.

1243
01:40:05,468 --> 01:40:07,629
Allan street, where is it?

1244
01:40:08,070 --> 01:40:11,471
Uh, allan, uh... It's, uh... it's uh...

1245
01:40:11,774 --> 01:40:15,710
It's 6 blocks up and, uh, 3 over.

1246
01:40:16,412 --> 01:40:19,074
You need any gas, father?

1247
01:42:06,322 --> 01:42:09,621
Oh, Jesus god. No.

1248
01:42:20,536 --> 01:42:22,731
Elaine!

1249
01:42:23,005 --> 01:42:25,565
Elaine!

1250
01:42:25,841 --> 01:42:28,173
Elaine!

1251
01:42:28,544 --> 01:42:30,842
Elaine!

1252
01:42:31,313 --> 01:42:33,577
Who is that guy? What's he doing?

1253
01:42:33,716 --> 01:42:35,877
- I' II take care of him. - He's too late.

1254
01:42:37,252 --> 01:42:39,413
Elaine!

1255
01:42:39,755 --> 01:42:45,921
Elaine! Elaine!

1256
01:42:46,528 --> 01:42:48,655
We've got to stop him!

1257
01:42:49,365 --> 01:42:57,795
Elaine! Elaine!

1258
01:43:06,682 --> 01:43:09,150
Ben!

1259
01:43:13,589 --> 01:43:16,251
You punk. You crazy punk!

1260
01:43:16,659 --> 01:43:18,286
I'll kill you.

1261
01:43:32,207 --> 01:43:34,175
Elaine! It 's too late!

1262
01:43:34,276 --> 01:43:35,766
Not for me!

1263
01:43:37,279 --> 01:43:41,443
- Move! Move! - Damn you!

